  "duration": 168.5536875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.56,
      "text": "Right now, the global conversation around artificial intelligence is a massive high-speed"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.56,
      "end": 8.26,
      "text": "collision of conflicting opinions and public panic."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.04,
      "end": 11.36,
      "text": "Here is a graphic of claims dominating the noise."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.18,
      "end": 15.96,
      "text": "Optimists insist the technology cures diseases and does boring tasks."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.64,
      "end": 19.46,
      "text": "Warriors are convinced it takes your job and hurts society."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.36,
      "end": 21.54,
      "text": "Daughters just roll their eyes."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.22,
      "end": 23.42,
      "text": "Which leaves the ultimate question."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.16,
      "end": 24.98,
      "text": "Who is actually right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.72,
      "end": 26.78,
      "text": "Here is the honest answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.52,
      "end": 27.86,
      "text": "Nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.86,
      "end": 32.2,
      "text": "Not the pundits, not us, and not even the engineers building the models."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.94,
      "end": 36.64,
      "text": "Because certainty about where this technology lands simply doesn't exist."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.24,
      "end": 39.46,
      "text": "Getting trapped in these arguments is a waste of time."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.08,
      "end": 43.04,
      "text": "Our actual job is figuring out how to navigate the blank space."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.7,
      "end": 45.98,
      "text": "Take a look at this map from the 1400s."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.4,
      "end": 49.34,
      "text": "The physical limits of the world were entirely unknown to explorers."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.18,
      "end": 51.94,
      "text": "But cartographers hated leaving a map blank."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.56,
      "end": 56.98,
      "text": "In the uncharted parts of the ocean, they projected their own terrors directly into the void."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.98,
      "end": 60.48,
      "text": "This illustration shows a terrifying sea monster."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.36,
      "end": 64.52,
      "text": "Today's AI warriors are doing the exact same thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.98,
      "end": 69.62,
      "text": "Filling the unknown map edges with monsters that destroy jobs and take over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.18,
      "end": 74.46,
      "text": "AI optimists look about identical uncharted water and predict clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.34,
      "end": 80.26,
      "text": "Those 15th century sailors rarely found sea monsters, or perfectly clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.1,
      "end": 82.24,
      "text": "Take Ferdinand the Jelen."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.6,
      "end": 84.46,
      "text": "He didn't set off to sail around the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.46,
      "end": 89.72,
      "text": "His crew achieved that milestone purely by reacting to unexpected obstacles along the way."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.54,
      "end": 92.28,
      "text": "And the reality of the unknown is harsh."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.02,
      "end": 94.92,
      "text": "Magellan died before the voyage even ended."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.66,
      "end": 99.9,
      "text": "We have exactly one factual certainty regarding our own unmapped future."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.64,
      "end": 101.78,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.42,
      "end": 103.16,
      "text": "It isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.86,
      "end": 108.48,
      "text": "To survive a technological shift of this scale, we have to take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.36,
      "end": 113.52,
      "text": "We reject both the panic of the sea monsters and the naivety of the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.52,
      "end": 115.94,
      "text": "And we prepare to react to the unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.84,
      "end": 121.22,
      "text": "Instead of historical philosophy, we need a concrete plan for your education."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.1,
      "end": 128.22,
      "text": "First, we tackle the argument, breaking down why voices disagree and how speed amplifies noise."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.06,
      "end": 134.42,
      "text": "Next, monsters and open water looks at valid worry alongside real world upside."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.3,
      "end": 142.06,
      "text": "Finally, where it lands on you examines how AI acts, your work, computing bills, and history's promise."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.06,
      "end": 146.58,
      "text": "The goal of this road map is not to successfully guess what happens next."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.3,
      "end": 151.08,
      "text": "The goal is to acquire the skills to be smarter than the tool right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.84,
      "end": 156.76,
      "text": "No expert, pundit, or engineer can hand you a finished, safe guide to this era."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.62,
      "end": 160.14,
      "text": "This final image leaves us with exactly one truth."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.96,
      "end": 162.46,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.14,
      "end": 164.96,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    }
  ],
